---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const rawBase = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const base = rawBase.endsWith('/') ? rawBase : `${rawBase}/`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Using AI for Research & Analysis — The AI Resource Hub"
  description="How to use AI to research topics, summarise documents, analyse data and fact-check, plus the pitfalls to avoid."
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-8 sm:py-12">
    <nav class="text-xs text-(--color-text-muted) mb-4" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href={base} class="hover:text-(--color-text-secondary) transition-colors">Home</a>
      <span class="mx-2">/</span>
      <a href={`${base}guides/`} class="hover:text-(--color-text-secondary) transition-colors">Guides</a>
      <span class="mx-2">/</span>
      <span class="text-(--color-text-secondary)">AI for Research</span>
    </nav>

    <header class="mb-10">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
        <span class="text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-purple-500/10 text-purple-400">Practical</span>
        <span class="text-xs text-(--color-text-muted)">10 min read</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-(--color-text-primary) mb-4">
        Using AI for Research & Analysis
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-(--color-text-secondary)">
        AI can be a useful research assistant, summarising documents, finding patterns, and helping you
        understand complex topics. But you need to know its limitations. Here's how to research effectively with AI.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-8">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-(--color-text-primary) mb-4">The Golden Rule: Trust but Verify</h2>
        <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-(--color-accent-glow) border border-(--color-accent)/20 mb-4">
          <p class="text-(--color-text-primary) leading-relaxed">
            <strong>AI models can and do make things up.</strong> They can cite books that don't exist, invent
            statistics, and state falsehoods with complete confidence. Never treat AI research output as fact
            without independent verification, especially dates, statistics, quotes, and scientific claims.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-(--color-text-primary) mb-4">Tools Worth Trying for Research</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-(--color-text-muted) mb-3">Features as described on each provider's own site, checked 26 Oct 2026. They change often.</p>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-(--color-bg-card) border border-(--color-border)">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-(--color-text-primary) mb-1">Perplexity AI</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-(--color-text-secondary)">A search-based answer engine that shows the web sources behind each answer. Useful for quick research and for finding pages to check. <a href="https://www.perplexity.ai/" rel="noopener" class="text-(--color-accent)">perplexity.ai</a></p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-(--color-bg-card) border border-(--color-border)">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-(--color-text-primary) mb-1">Gemini Deep Research</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-(--color-text-secondary)">Google says it can browse hundreds of websites and write a multi-page report in minutes. Useful when you want a first survey of a topic, but check the citations. <a href="https://gemini.google/overview/deep-research/" rel="noopener" class="text-(--color-accent)">Google's overview</a></p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-(--color-bg-card) border border-(--color-border)">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-(--color-text-primary) mb-1">Claude</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-(--color-text-secondary)">You can upload a PDF or other long document and ask detailed questions about it. Useful for document analysis. Limits per model are in our <a href={`${base}context-window/`} class="text-(--color-accent)">context window table</a>.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-(--color-bg-card) border border-(--color-border)">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-(--color-text-primary) mb-1">ChatGPT search</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-(--color-text-secondary)">Searches the web from inside a chat and links its sources. Good for general research that needs recent information. <a href="https://openai.com/index/introducing-chatgpt-search/" rel="noopener" class="text-(--color-accent)">OpenAI's announcement</a></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-(--color-text-primary) mb-4">Research Workflows</h2>

        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-(--color-text-primary) mb-3">Summarising a Long Document</h3>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-(--color-bg-card) border border-(--color-border) mb-4">
          <ol class="text-sm text-(--color-text-secondary) space-y-2 list-decimal list-inside">
            <li>Upload the document (PDF, paste text, or share a link)</li>
            <li>Ask for a high-level summary first: "Summarise the key points of this document in 5 bullet points"</li>
            <li>Then drill into specific sections: "What does section 3 say about [topic]?"</li>
            <li>Extract structured data: "Create a table of all recommendations with their rationale"</li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-(--color-text-primary) mb-3">Learning a New Topic</h3>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-(--color-bg-card) border border-(--color-border) mb-4">
          <ol class="text-sm text-(--color-text-secondary) space-y-2 list-decimal list-inside">
            <li>Start broad: "Explain [topic] like I'm a smart 15-year-old"</li>
            <li>Get the landscape: "What are the 5 most important things to understand about [topic]?"</li>
            <li>Go deeper: "Now explain [specific aspect] in more detail"</li>
            <li>Test understanding: "I think [your understanding]. Am I right, or what am I missing?"</li>
            <li>Get resources: "What are the best books/articles/courses to learn more about this?"</li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-(--color-text-primary) mb-3">Competitive Analysis</h3>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-(--color-bg-card) border border-(--color-border) mb-4">
          <p class="text-sm text-(--color-text-secondary) italic">
            "I run a [type of business] in [location]. My main competitors are [list them].
            Analyse their strengths and weaknesses compared to us. Present as a comparison table
            with columns for: Company, Strengths, Weaknesses, Pricing, and Unique Selling Point.
            Use information you know about these companies, and clearly flag anything you're not sure about."
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-(--color-text-primary) mb-4">Common Mistakes</h2>
        <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3">
          <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-red-500/5 border border-red-500/20">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-red-400 text-sm mb-2">Don't</h3>
            <ul class="text-sm text-(--color-text-secondary) space-y-1">
              <li>Trust AI statistics without checking</li>
              <li>Use AI citations without verifying they exist</li>
              <li>Ask one model and treat it as definitive</li>
              <li>Rely on AI for medical, legal, or financial advice</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-green-500/5 border border-green-500/20">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-green-400 text-sm mb-2">Do</h3>
            <ul class="text-sm text-(--color-text-secondary) space-y-1">
              <li>Cross-reference key claims with real sources</li>
              <li>Ask AI to flag things it's uncertain about</li>
              <li>Use AI to find leads, then verify yourself</li>
              <li>Prefer tools that show their sources, and open them</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8">
      <a
        href={`${base}guides/`}
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2 rounded-lg bg-(--color-bg-tertiary) text-(--color-text-secondary) hover:text-(--color-text-primary) hover:bg-(--color-bg-hover) transition-colors text-sm"
      >
        <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" />
        </svg>
        All Guides
      </a>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
